Assistant: # Removing Duplicate Characters from a String in JavaScript

Here are several approaches, from most modern to most manual:

## 1. Using `Set` (Recommended)

```javascript
function removeDuplicates(str) {
  return [...new Set(str)].join('');
}

console.log(removeDuplicates("hello"));      // "helo"
console.log(removeDuplicates("programming")); // "progamin"
```

**How it works:**
- `[...str]` spreads the string into an array of characters
- `new Set(...)` keeps only unique values
- `.join('')` converts back to a string

## 2. Using `filter` + `indexOf`

```javascript
function removeDuplicates(str) {
  return [...str].filter((char, index) => str.indexOf(char) === index).join('');
}
```

**How it works:**
- Keeps a character only if its first occurrence matches the current index

## 3. Using a `for` loop (most manual)

```javascript
function removeDuplicates(str) {
  let result = '';
  for (const char of str) {
    if (!result.includes(char)) {
      result += char;
    }
  }
  return result;
}
```

## 4. Using `reduce`

```javascript
function removeDuplicates(str) {
  return [...str].reduce((acc, char) => {
    return acc.includes(char) ? acc : acc + char;
  }, '');
}
```

---

## Comparison

| Approach | Time Complexity | Readability |
|----------|----------------|-------------|
| `Set` | O(n) | ⭐⭐⭐ |
| `filter` + `indexOf` | O(n²) | ⭐⭐ |
| `for` loop | O(n²) | ⭐⭐ |
| `reduce` | O(n²) | ⭐⭐ |

